// %git at madc -i (split arc 1B.10, design
// 2026-10-10-git-module-command-design.md): the madcgit module, loaded by
// -lmadcgit, brings %git into the session's registry; each verb prints what
// git prints for the same question over the repository the test runs in
// (every lane runs the suite from a checkout root), asserted by SHAPE —
// never a sha or a count history would move: status (git status -sb's
// `## BRANCH`), log (git log --format='%h %s (%ar, %an)'), show REV (the
// commit's header) and REV:FILE (the file at REV), blame FILE:LINE (git
// blame --date=relative's `SHA8 (AUTHOR DATE LINE) TEXT`), diff FILE (an
// unchanged file prints nothing); the refusals (diagnostics: their texts are
// test_gitrepo's), %git's row in %help.
int main(void) { return 0; }
